  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s A285 drawing of Bourgoin’s plate 149 (top): a sixteen-pointed star on a square tile, eight-pointed stars on the tile’s sides and a four-pointed star at each corner, every star split into kites. Every edge runs at a multiple of 11.25°. The star’s lines join points of its circle 90° apart. The tile’s half-side is the one free length (drawing: 1.97067 times the star’s radius); we take the crossing of the 45° line through A with the chord from U3 to S7, 1.97086. Every other line runs through a crossing of earlier lines. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. The tile is 0.01% larger than Wichmann’s (0.024 pt in his drawing). Wichmann colours each piece and its mirror image differently; we colour by shape. No photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
